{"headline":"September ending cash decreased by $620,000, driven by lower settled collections and higher settled outflows; three September-expected customer receipts remained open.","narrative":"Northstar settled cash for CASH-US Operating ••1842 closed at $2.58 million on September 30, down from $3.20 million at August 31. The bank statement reconciles September activity to $2.23 million of settled credits and $2.85 million of settled debits, or net cash outflow of $620,000. August had $2.85 million of settled credits and $2.55 million of settled debits, or net inflow of $300,000. Thus, month-over-month net cash generation deteriorated by $920,000: settled credits decreased by $620,000 and settled debits increased by $300,000. The September debit increase includes a $300,000 annual identity-platform renewal to Okta / WorkOS Bundle; the statements alone establish the payment and amount, not accounting or business causation.

The ERP identified $620,000 of September-expected receipts that remained open at September 30: NovaWorks INV-NW-1042 ($240,000), BluePeak INV-BP-2088 ($210,000), and HarborLine INV-HL-3301 ($170,000). These are recorded receivables/expected receipts—not settled cash. The September bank statement does not show matching named customer credits for them. NovaWorks' authorized AP API corroborates that its invoice was pending approval after an initial missing-PO rejection, with no remittance or payment scheduled. BluePeak's portal shows the invoice as disputed after legal-entity-mismatch rejections. The later human resolutions selected the customer-portal entity assertion for this issue and resolved the BluePeak conflict; the underlying books assertion remains preserved as historical source evidence. HarborLine's AP-desk statement that the invoice was in procurement review is communication evidence only and remains provisional; the ERP confirms only that it was open and had no remittance.

Accordingly, the cash decline is verified at the bank level. The evidence supports lower settled collections and higher settled disbursements as the quantitative cash bridge. Operational explanations for the expected-but-unsettled receivables are customer-specific status evidence, and do not establish that the receipts settled.","claims":[{"key":"ending_cash","text":"Northstar settled cash closed at $2.58 million on September 30 versus $3.20 million on August 31, a $620,000 decrease.","confidence":"verified","assertion_ids":["ast-a82f48a3197a","ast-f67e45679b1e","ast-a9f7c1ba9c6d"]},{"key":"cash_bridge","text":"September had $2.23 million of settled credits and $2.85 million of settled debits, compared with August $2.85 million credits and $2.55 million debits. Net cash generation therefore changed from +$300,000 to -$620,000, a $920,000 deterioration.","confidence":"verified","assertion_ids":["ast-d88ce2a2b18f","ast-a9f7c1ba9c6d"]},{"key":"collections_vs_outflows","text":"The month-over-month bridge consists of a $620,000 reduction in settled credits and a $300,000 increase in settled debits. This is a cash-flow comparison, not a causal attribution.","confidence":"verified","assertion_ids":["ast-d88ce2a2b18f","ast-a9f7c1ba9c6d"]},{"key":"identity_renewal","text":"The September statement includes a settled $300,000 debit to Okta / WorkOS Bundle described as an annual identity-platform renewal.","confidence":"verified","assertion_ids":["ast-a9f7c1ba9c6d"]},{"key":"open_expected_receipts","text":"ERP reported three open CASH-US invoices expected in September totaling $620,000: NovaWorks $240,000, BluePeak $210,000, and HarborLine $170,000. These are expected receipts/open AR and are not described as settled cash.","confidence":"verified","assertion_ids":["ast-a91d8738bbdb","ast-7d9aaaf69cb2","ast-d4183058bc3a","ast-07d0a71a2acc","ast-df289626eeb6","ast-aabef699ad39","ast-f2052667af8e","ast-a8e38a91ceb2"]},{"key":"novaworks_context","text":"NovaWorks INV-NW-1042 was pending approval after a missing-PO issue; its AP API returned no September remittance and no payment schedule. This corroborates operational nonpayment status, not bank settlement.","confidence":"corroborated","assertion_ids":["ast-9453ca263527","ast-2486893a93de","ast-3e11f97fb744"]},{"key":"bluepeak_context","text":"BluePeak INV-BP-2088 was shown as disputed after two legal-entity-mismatch rejections. The human resolutions selected the portal-side entity determination and closed the material entity conflict; historic ERP and portal assertions are preserved.","confidence":"corroborated","assertion_ids":["ast-140f62777757","ast-c68fa9cc0f77","ast-166bfc9758c1","ast-881ec16dc13c","ast-21e8fd0df4b1"]},{"key":"harborline_context","text":"HarborLine INV-HL-3301 was open in ERP. The AP desk's procurement-review explanation and follow-up promise are provisional communication claims; they are not settlement evidence.","confidence":"provisional","assertion_ids":["ast-f2052667af8e","ast-a8e38a91ceb2","ast-f7d97b98301b","ast-27c8b2b9e989","ast-1c6cc94381aa"]}],"open_conflicts":[],"unknowns":["No post-September bank evidence was obtained to determine whether any of the three invoices subsequently settled.","No bank settlement is inferred from ERP, API, portal, or voice evidence.","HarborLine's stated procurement-review reason and timing remain uncorroborated communication evidence.","The bank statements establish cash movement, but do not independently establish the accounting classification or business purpose of the payments."],"drivers":[{"label":"Decrease in settled collections versus August","amount_cents":-62000000,"confidence":"verified","assertion_ids":["ast-d88ce2a2b18f","ast-a9f7c1ba9c6d"]},{"label":"Increase in settled debits versus August","amount_cents":-30000000,"confidence":"verified","assertion_ids":["ast-d88ce2a2b18f","ast-a9f7c1ba9c6d"]},{"label":"Open September-expected customer receipts (not settled cash)","amount_cents":62000000,"confidence":"verified","assertion_ids":["ast-a91d8738bbdb","ast-7d9aaaf69cb2"]}]}

